 "summary": "Charles Leclerc won a chaotic British Grand Prix by 0.427s from George Russell, with Ferrari team mate Lewis Hamilton 0.772s back, delivering Ferrari's 250th F1 win. The race featured two VSC periods, for an umbrella and Nico Hulkenberg's issue, before Max Verstappen crashed at Stowe and brought out a late Safety Car that stayed out to the flag. Antonelli led after the pit cycle but a left-front wheel-shield failure forced two stops; Russell's slow puncture and a late stay-out gamble delivered second, while Antonelli's title lead was cut to 25 points. Verstappen, Alexander Albon and Hulkenberg retired; Hamilton's false-start five-second penalty and Sainz's post-race penalty lap were applied.",
 "classification": [
